12075	{"type":"command_lifecycle","command_uuid":"b8da880f-295c-49f4-ae25-38a625ddb632","state":"queued","uuid":"9e0a4285-975f-4631-9834-6261088df5a5","session_id":"f5ad2a8d-7a8c-4a8a-a6d3-9ae6efaf063b"}
12159	{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoXC8gfx9ejasfajihn4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Lighthouses\n\nA lighthouse is a tall tower built at a coastline, on a reef, or on a headland to warn ships of hazards and guide them toward safe harbors. Its height matters because light must reach over the curve of the Earth to be seen from far away. Keepers once tended the flame, trimmed wicks, and polished lenses through the night. The tower's position, shape, and paint pattern also helped sailors recognize it by day.\n\nThe heart of a traditional lighthouse is its lens, usually a Fresnel lens invented in the 1820s. Instead of one thick piece of glass, it uses concentric rings of prisms that bend light into a narrow, powerful beam. This design captures far more of the lamp's output than older mirrors did. A single modest flame, magnified this way, could be seen from twenty miles or more across open water.\n\nEach lighthouse needs a distinct identity, so mariners know which one they are seeing. This is called its characteristic. The lens assembly rotates, or shutters open and close, to produce a pattern of flashes and dark intervals. One tower might flash once every ten seconds, while another shows two quick flashes then a pause. Charts list these patterns, letting navigators confirm their position. Some lights also use colored glass to mark channels or dangers.\n\nModern lighthouses have largely become automated. Electric lamps, LEDs, and solar panels replaced oil and keepers, and many now run unattended with remote monitoring. Radar beacons, foghorns, and GPS supplement the light, especially in poor visibility. Although satellite navigation has reduced dependence on them, lighthouses still serve as reliable backups that need no signal or software. Many are preserved as museums and heritage landmarks, remembering the long era of seafaring."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":135,"cache_read_input_tokens":17085,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":135},"output_tokens":575,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5ad2a8d-7a8c-4a8a-a6d3-9ae6efaf063b","uuid":"5298988d-31aa-4d24-a1f3-53fbe15fc26b","timestamp":"2026-11-07T11:53:14.994Z","request_id":"req_011CgoXC8GdAHwEzELVjebWD"}
